/**
 * categories_data.js — curated collections behind the «التصنيفات» nav entries.
 *
 * The upstream TMDB cache exposes NO genre / country filter (documented in
 * api.js): list rows carry no `genre_ids`, and only ?action=movie|tv&id= does.
 * These three sets were therefore resolved title-by-title against that endpoint
 * and frozen here, exactly like catalog_data.js / tv_catalog.js, so the anime,
 * Asian and Turkish screens render instantly — and still render when the
 * upstream answers {"error": "..."} (Cloudflare 403) because no request is
 * needed.
 *
 * Membership rules (applied when each list was generated):
 *   anime   — TMDB genre 16 (Animation) AND Japanese language / JP origin.
 *   asian   — Japanese, Korean, Chinese, Hindi, Thai, Filipino… original
 *             language (or origin country) but NOT animation, so the screens
 *             never repeat: Japanese anime lives only in `anime`, and Turkey
 *             (west Asia) is not part of it.
 *   turkish — original language `tr` (or origin country TR), not animation and
 *             not an Asian language; it is its own screen, never a repeat of
 *             `asian`.
 *   Persia (`fa`) stays out of scope entirely.
 *
 * Row shape matches the list rows of the API (see api.js normaliseRow), so the
 * pages consume them through exactly the same code path as live data.
 * Rows are pre-sorted by rating — that is the default order of each screen.
 */

